@startsalt
!include https://raw.githubusercontent.com/proveo-ca/identity/main/proveo.puml
' purpose: PROPOSED — the screens `proveo init` shows when it provisions credentials, before any of it is agreed
' PROPOSAL, not shipped behaviour. The plan it draws: _spec/_plans/init-credential-provisioning.puml
'   the form this reuses ....... _spec/internal/choiceui/wireframe.puml
'   where a secret rests ....... _spec/_plans/secret-custody.puml
'   what the agent may hold .... _spec/_paradigms/credential-boundary.puml
'   the store's two names ...... _spec/internal/sbx/credential-path.puml
'
' ── WHAT THIS EXISTS TO FIX ────────────────────────────────────────────────
' Measured 2026-09-16 on a fedora host with no credential of any kind: every
' def reached its login prompt and exited there, ~10s per run, and the operator
' read it as a crash. proveo said the true thing twice in the same output —
' "running anyway; the agent will handle login", then "the sbx backend cannot
' complete a login" — which is a contradiction a reader resolves by disbelieving
' both. The Keychain that holds the macOS answer is darwin-only by design, so
' there is no equivalent surface on linux to point at.
'
' `sbx setup` is not that surface either: it imports what the host already
' exports and prompts for nothing, so an operator holding a key in their head
' has nowhere to type it.
'
' ── THE ONE RULE THESE SCREENS OBEY ────────────────────────────────────────
' A secret is never drawn, never echoed, never an argv word, and never written
' to a file proveo owns. The form collects the DECISION; the value is read after
' the form exits, with echo off, and goes straight to `sbx secret set` on stdin.
' That is why the key entry below is a separate screen rather than a row: salt
' can draw a password field, and a TUI row that accepts one would be the first
' place proveo held key material in its own process longer than a write.
'
' ── A CREDENTIAL IS NOT A PRECONDITION, AND THIS SCREEN DOES NOT PRETEND IT IS
' Operator's question, 2026-09-16: why are credentials necessary? They are not.
' An agent launches without one and shows its own login screen, which is the
' flow every harness ships. What proveo cannot do TODAY is keep that login:
' measured the same day, `proveo_sync_state` walks `_proveo_volume_state_dirs`,
' which reads /proc/mounts for /dev-backed mounts under the agent home. Under
' docker those are volumes and the walk finds them; under sbx the home is a VM
' path with nothing /dev-backed beneath it, so the walk yields nothing and the
' state sync is a NO-OP. A `/login` completed inside an sbx run is discarded
' with the sandbox.
'
' So this screen offers provisioning; it does not gate the run on it. The
' refusal an operator meets today — "the sbx backend cannot complete a login" —
' is a statement about that no-op, not about agents, and it retires when the
' state sync learns where an sbx home keeps its state.
'
' ── THE LIST IS FILTERED BY THE AGENT, NOT BY THE REGISTRY ─────────────────
' Operator's rule: show what the relevant agent can actually use, subscription
' first. Two shapes follow, because two kinds of def exist:
'   NARROW def — claudecode, codex, cursor. One vendor, one plan. Its own
'                subscription is the top row, named as the thing it is (`/login`
'                inside the agent, or the env var that carries the same token),
'                and the api key for that same vendor sits under it.
'   BROAD def  — opencode, cecli. Many providers, none privileged. The short
'                list: providers a def runs on, plus any whose key is already on
'                this host. The other two dozen the registry knows are reachable
'                through `sbx secret set` and named in the footer.
'
' A row per variable would ask the operator to know that CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN
' and ANTHROPIC_API_KEY are one provider in two kinds. The row is the provider;
' the KIND is the option; the store name follows from the pair.

title PROPOSED · `proveo init` credential stage — screen 1: filtered by the agent, subscription first

{
{+
  {
    <&terminal> proveo SOLUTIONS | proveo/sandbox: portable, safe AI coding agents
  }
  ==credentials for claudecode — a narrow def: one vendor, subscription first
  {
    host: | linux/amd64 · sbx 0.42.0 · KVM present
    store: | sbx secret store — host-wide, outlives every run, the agent never holds it
    without one: | <color:#9a9a9a>the agent still launches and shows its own login — it is the NEXT run that forgets it
  }
  ~~
  {
    . | leave | provide | .
    . | . | ———— subscription ———— | .
    ▸ claudecode | ( ) | (X) /login in the agent | <color:#9a9a9a>— `proveo run claudecode`, then /login; proveo never sees the token
    . | . | ( ) CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN | <color:#9a9a9a>— `claude setup-token` on this host, stored as `claudecode`
    . | . | ———— api key ———— | .
    anthropic | (X) leave as is | ( ) api key | <color:#00BAC6>— sbx store: anthropic, ANTHROPIC_API_KEY
  }
  --
  ↑↓ row · ↔ move · enter accept · esc cancel — nothing is written until you accept
  ..
  every other provider: `sbx secret set <service>` · one sbx does not know: `sbx secret set-custom --host <api-host> --env <VAR>`
}
{
{^"1 · a BROAD def — opencode, cecli — gets the short list"
  . | ———— subscription ————
  opencode | ( ) leave | (X) api key
  . | ———— api keys ————
  anthropic | (X) leave as is | ( ) api key
  openai | (X) leave as is | ( ) api key
  google | ( ) leave | (X) api key
  .
  No vendor is privileged, so the top row
  is the def's own plan and the rest are
  the providers it can route to: def-backed,
  plus any key already on this host. The
  other two dozen stay in the footer.
}
{^"2 · an env-carried key is amber, not green"
  opencode | ( ) leave | (X) api key
  .
  <color:#E8A33D>this host's env only: OPENCODE_API_KEY</color>
  .
  It works today and keeps working — the
  retirement is additive first. Drawing it
  as a pass is what leaves an operator
  believing the store is populated when
  one `unset` empties it.
}
{^"3 · already stored — the row still appears"
  cursor | (X) leave as is | ( ) api key
  .
  <color:#00BAC6>sbx store: cursor</color>
  .
  A provisioned provider is not dropped:
  the list is where an operator checks
  what this host can spend, and an absent
  row answers no question.
}
{^"4 · no TTY — the form is eliminated, the report is not"
  . | secrets
  . | anthropic — sbx store: anthropic
  . | opencode — this host's env only
  . | <color:#9a9a9a>not a terminal — run `proveo init` from a shell to provision
  .
  Every path still REPORTS. Only the
  asking needs a terminal.
}
{^"5 · the two kinds never share one store id"
  claudecode | (X) /login | ( ) token
  anthropic | (X) leave as is | ( ) api key
  .
  A subscription stores as `claudecode`,
  the key as `anthropic`. One id cannot
  carry both: a proxy attaching an OAuth
  token into an x-api-key header answers
  401 to a credential that is good. Where
  a def is NAMED for its provider, its
  subscription takes `<service>-sub`.
}
}
}
@endsalt
